6. Engine Control System Software Overview
An Engine Control System primarily comprises of following components: EEC, Sensors, Embedded Software, Fuel
Control Unit (FCU), Handling Bleed-Off Valve (HBOV), Variable Inlet Guide Vanes (VIGV), Igniters, Shutdown
Solenoid(s), Wiring Harness, Data Collection Unit (DCU), and other items. Main functions of the Engine Control
System include automated start/shutdown sequencing, fuel flow modulation in response to pilot commands,
automated surge/flameout avoidance, limiting of engine power, speed, torque, and temperature parameters as
appropriate and the serial data interface to the aircraft displays and avionics system.
