Control System Software Development Process Requirements
This section provides control system software development process requirements including software processes,
procedures, standards, activities and products that are applied to the AS CSCI of engine control system.
Control System Software Development Life Cycle Model
The P&WC engine control systems software development process employs a “V” model with evolutionary iterative
(incremental) life cycle in the development of its software as shown in Figure 3. This model consists of a sequential
progression through a series of development phases, with each phase building on the outputs of the previous
phase and verified through the corresponding transition criteria review process in accordance with RTCA/
DO-178B/C and DAPM. Transition criteria during each phase include, Input documents (or data) required to enter
into life cycle phase (Entry-Criteria), activities performed during the phase, and output documents required exiting
from the life cycle phase (Exit-Criteria) to enter into subsequent development phase in the life cycle.(e.g.
transitioning from Software Requirements phase to Software Design phase).
