Control System Software Planning Process Activities
Software planning process includes the Plan for Software Aspects of Certification (PSAC), the Software
Development Plan (SDP) including the Software Development Standards, the Software Verification Plan (SVP), the
Software Configuration Management Plan (SCMP) and the Software Quality Assurance Plan (SQAP). These
documents are produced as per the roles and responsibilities defined in the PSAC and shall conform to the
guidelines in RTCA/DO-178B/C and the requirements stated hereafter.
The PSAC is reviewed by Software DAA or CVE to ensure that it meets the guidance of DO-178B/C. The PSAC
must be approved by Software DAA or CVE before it can be submitted to certification authorities and prior to any
formal software design activities being undertaken.
In the event that product security functionality is to be incorporated in the software, the associated PSAC shall also
be approved by the Product Security DAA (PS DAA) or the cognizant Software CVE with product security aspects
knowledge.
Software Development Standards
The software development standards include the software requirements standards, software design standards and
software coding standards. These standards are applicable to AS-CL described in Section 6 for P&WC
deliverables. The P&WC design team shall be responsible to ensure that these standards are aligned with software
design tools and processes defined in PSAC and SDP, respectively.
Software Requirements Standards
The AS-CL high-level requirements are developed in compliance with Software Requirements Standards. Refer to
the program specific PSAC for details on software development environment. Software Requirements Standards
shall conform to the guidelines in RTCA/DO-178B/C section 11.6. WIM 493 (Preparation And Use Of The Software
Requirements Document (SRD)) and MED 293 or MED 267 (NGPF Programs) provides guidance on writing
software requirements.
Software Design Standards
The AS design (low-level requirements) is performed in compliance with the Software Design Standards. Refer to
the program specific PSAC for details on software development environment. The Software Design Standards shall
conform to the guidelines specified in RTCA/DO-178B/C Section 11.7.
Software Design Standards
The AS architecture is performed in compliance with the software architecture standards in WIM 795.
Software Coding Standards
The AS code is generated using automatic code generator tool and manual code in compliance with the Software
Coding Standards as defined in the SDP. Refer to the program specific PSAC for software development
environment. The Software Coding Standards shall conform to the guidelines specified in RTCA/DO-178B/C
Section 11.8.
Software Development Tools
Software development tools for which certification credit is sought for shall be qualified. Refer to program specific
PSAC for a description of such tools.
