Process Tailoring for Transition Criteria Reviews
Tailoring of the definition of transition criteria and the corresponding review process shall be permitted by the
Manager Software Design team in accordance with the nature and purpose of the software being developed for an
engine program. Tailoring of this process consists of the following:
• Identifying transition criteria review requirements that are not applicable.
• Adding transition criteria review requirements.
• Providing quantifiable criteria for the transition criteria review requirements (how often, how many, transition
criteria, etc.).
Approved (by DAA/Certification authority) process tailoring has to be documented either in program specific PSAC
or P&WC internal process document and will be communicated to the affected engineering groups.
